  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Wednesday...\n\nA weak upper wave drops through the Northern Rockies today.\nSprinkles to light showers may continue through this afternoon \nacross portions of south-central Montana. Accumulations are\nexpected to be very light with any activity. A backdoor cold front\nthis afternoon will help keep temperatures cool with highs in the\n50s and 60sF. Winds will increase out of the east to northeast as\nwell, with gusts in the teens to low 20s mph mainly around and\neast of Billings. A weak low-level jet develops tonight over the\nsoutheast, with gusts in the 20s mph as well.\n\nOtherwise, riding and dry conditions will build Friday into the\nweekend, lasting into next week. High temperatures climb back into\nthe 70s to around 80F for Friday, before another dry cold front\nbriefly drops temperatures into the upper 60s to low 70sF on \nSaturday. Highs will return to the 70s to 80s Sunday into the \nmiddle of next week, with Monday looking to be the warmest day.\n\nAn additional cold front may bring temperatures down a touch on\nTuesday, though the latest forecast keeps highs in the mid to\nupper 70sF anyway. High confidence remains for above normal \ntemperatures and dry conditions through the first half of next \nweek, with ensembles agreeing that ridging will continue through\nthe end of next week.\n\nMatos",
